Example builds
==============

From the repository root
```bash
make -C examples/grammar                          # Run grammar tests
make -C examples/farrow-lv sched                  # Schedule APS modules
make -C examples/bigger bigger-binding.sched      # or using .sched alias
make -C examples/farrow-lv scala EVALUATOR=STATIC
make -C examples scala                            # Build all Scala drivers
make -C examples test                             # Run configured tests
```

Each folder contains one AST and its build configuration.

- `ast.mk`: names the folder's single AST source:

```Makefile
AST = tiny.aps
```

- `Makefile`: sets the folder's build and test options

```Makefile
include ast.mk
SCALA_DRIVERS             Drivers to build
TEST_DRIVERS              Drivers to test
TEST_PROGRAMS             Space-separated input globs, relative to examples/scala
TEST_EVALUATORS           Evaluators to compare (default: DYNAMIC,STATIC)
TEST_EVALUATORS_<Driver>  Optional per-driver override
SCHED_MODULES             Modules to schedule (default: all .aps except AST)
include ../common.mk
```

- `scala.mk`: Describes the Scala build:

```Makefile
include ../<module>/ast.mk
SOURCES.<module>          APS and handwritten Scala inputs for one output module
SHARED_SOURCES            Source files shared by output modules
DRIVERS                   Driver names; append with +=
DRIVER.<name>             APS module file, optionally followed by name of main Scala object
TREE_MODULES              AST module names, generated without evaluator flags
MODULE_CONFIG             Rebuild dependencies (default: source folder's scala.mk and ast.mk)
PARSER_BASENAME           Prefix for generated scanner, parser, and token classes
LEXER / PARSER            .lex and .y input files, if the example has a parser
```
